\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Coarse-grained geometry of the hydrothermal vent model. The physical object is a porous mineral chimney or vent wall separating hot reduced vent fluid from colder ocean water. The one-dimensional coordinate is an effective coordinate through this porous reactive wall, not an empty line in the ocean. Each model cell represents a slice of water-filled mineral pores with local temperature, pH, flow, dissolved chemistry, and reactive mineral surface area such as FeS or NiS. Pore and surface chemistry happen first; coacervates and vesicle-like objects are later products of that chemistry. }}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
